calar Triple Product" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050356 #edb/ref 1033 1286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050356 #edb/ref 1034 1.224438375983708 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050356 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "421dabda-4549-5ad6-b909-e9e0b37e1c41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186105729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428198 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1031 "Calculating the Magnitude of Cartesian Vectors in 3D" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1033 1277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1034 0.7167474973411709 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051021 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7ab3215d-4ce4-5e76-8672-0d6b5580e957" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105596 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4350" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105596 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105596 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b3be2b13-b455-5dde-accf-259c075e1e1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105596 #edb/ref 1074 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105597 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4351" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105597 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105597 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c6f2dacc-11b0-5689-97d9-e1869c64aae1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105597 #edb/ref 1074 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105598 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4352" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105598 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105598 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4deee6cc-69e4-5da4-9c78-57bf6c988500" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105598 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105907 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105907 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105907 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105907 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186106310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105907 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105907 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105907 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186287822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105907 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 1759218629516